    "dev": {
      "added acl:read:code-mirror": "git.mirror (KD-9200, review 04.11.2026): dev reads the bare copy of the code mirror its forge executor fetched — read only, no network, no key",
      "added additionalDirectories:/srv/digipaddock-mirror": "git.mirror: the same copy, so git fetch github reads it by path inside the sandbox",
      "added channel:self:digi-dev:kd-mirror-fetch *": "git.mirror: kd-mirror-fetch <branch> asks the forge executor (its own read-only deploy key, the mirror's pinned host key) to fetch one branch into the copy; replaces the sandbox's network to the mirror host",
      "added channel:self:digi-dev:kd-data *": "data.read (KD-211, owner 05.11.2026): kd-data <database> <SQL> asks the data executor for one read-only statement; dev holds no key and no network",
      "added channel:data:digi-data:kd-data": "data.read: the data user alone holds the data key; on the server its forced command is the gate's MySQL-only mode (one checked SELECT/SHOW/EXPLAIN/DESCRIBE, no secret columns, 30 s, 1 MB, masked), every call journaled",
      "added allow:Edit(//srv/digipaddock-agents/dev/memory/chats/**)": "KD-9046: the session's own notes of a chat thread, inside the agent's own memory folder (Edit of memory/notes.md, the shared notes, is denied instead)",
      "added allow:Edit(//srv/digipaddock-agents/dev/memory/tasks/**)": "KD-9046: the session's own notes of a card, inside the agent's own memory folder",
      "added channel:self:digi-dev:kd-work council": "KD-9267: read-only — the council of models of a card the agent may see, as a paged text (its rounds, the critics' findings, the writer's answers); through the base executor like every kd-work form",
      "added channel:self:digi-dev:kd-work council-reply": "KD-9267: the writer's answers to the findings of its own card's council — the executor refuses anyone but the writer in the turn the cabinet started for it; writes the answers only, no card field",
      "added channel:self:digi-dev:kd-notes add": "KD-9046: appends one entry to the agent's own memory/notes.md under a lock, as the agent's own user; the sandbox no longer writes that file",
      "added channel:self:digi-dev:kd-forge status": "KD-9337: read-only — the checks (commit statuses) of one commit of a registered project by its hash, the merged one too, so the developer sees the deploy its merge started; the forge executor reads them with the dev account's token, as kd-forge pr does; nothing is written"
    },
    "sysadmin": {
      "added channel:self:digi-sysadmin:kd-monitor keys": "KD-9193: read-only lookup of SSH key fingerprints in the monitor's own snapshots and baseline identities, under the agent's own user like kd-monitor list",
      "added channel:self:digi-sysadmin:kd-monitor revoke": "KD-9272: only proposes a monitor_trust decision «доступ снят» for a login by a key, like kd-monitor accept; changes nothing until the owner signs it, and then the monitor closes the P-n without trusting the key, only if its snapshot shows the key no longer allowed",
